<title>RUSSIA: Russia LUKoil up near 4 pct for day.</title>
<headline>Russia LUKoil up near 4 pct for day.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Russia's largest oil producer NK LUKoil  had risen almost four percent to $15.42 by 1245 GMT from $14.85 at Friday's close on the Russian Trading System.</p>
<p>Atlantic Richfield Corporation (ARCO) and LUKoil signed a joint venture pact late on Friday that LUKoil said was worth $5 billion.</p>
<p>LUKoil represents about $11 billion of the Russian shares markets' approximately $54 billion capitalisation, equity analysts say.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
